From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:59:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "pixel: Restore drv2624 vibrator HAL APEX"

This reverts commit 58b562a3, restoring b2e5214f.

Upstream dropped the drv2624 vibrator HAL with "Reason for revert: Only
used by wahoo and bonito" -- not because anything was wrong with it.
bonito is one of those two, and it is the Pixel 3a's 2018 haptic driver,
so without this there is no haptic feedback at all.

This restores the whole set LineageOS themselves curated: vibrator/
Android.bp with PixelVibratorBinaryDefaults, vibrator/common, and
vibrator/drv2624. It is the AIDL HAL packaged as the
com.android.vibrator.drv2624 APEX, the same shape lineage-22.2 ships and
where haptics work on this device. It declares vibrator AIDL v2 and
compatibility_matrix.7.xml -- the FCM level this device targets --
accepts 1-2, so no version bump is needed, and the sepolicy it names
under hardware/google/pixel-sepolicy/vibrator still exists upstream.

